# Lane BE-1 work log (append-only)

## Phase 1 — SSE event coverage (auditD)

- Added the 6 published-but-filtered types (`form.created/replied/cancelled`,
  `shell.created/exited/deleted`) + the 14 unpublished types to the oc-core bus
  registry NON_SESSION list (constants appended; existing positional accessors
  unaffected). `is_public_event` now admits all 20 (oc-server/src/sse.rs:157).
- Ref citations for the 14 (schemas + emission points found in /opt/opencode-ref):
  - session.status / session.idle — schema/src/session-status-event.ts:35-53.
    No publisher exists in the ref snapshot; consumers derive busy/idle from
    session.execution.* (client/src/solid/data.ts:1009-1037). Port publishes
    busy on execution start, idle on settle, matching that union.
  - filesystem.changed {file, event:add|change|unlink} — schema/filesystem.ts;
    sole ref publisher core/src/filesystem/location-watcher.ts:28-32 (watches
    <gitdir>/HEAD only).
  - vcs.branch.updated {branch?} — schema/vcs-event.ts; publisher
    core/src/vcs.ts:148 (refresh after HEAD change).
  - worktree.updated {projectID} — schema/worktree.ts:55-58; publisher
    core/src/worktree.ts:131 (create/remove/refresh with update=true).
  - credential.updated {} / credential.switched {integrationID, credentialID} —
    schema/credential.ts:17-24; publishers core/src/credential.ts:160,163,202,
    253,313,316 (global:true).
  - models-dev.refreshed {} — schema/models-dev.ts:5-8; publisher
    core/src/models-dev.ts:422 (after digest-changed refresh).
  - tui.prompt.append/command.execute/toast.show/session.select —
    schema/tui-event.ts; ref-TUI consumes from the stream (tui/src/app.tsx:
    1253-1274); publisher = plugin host / external.
  - installation.updated / installation.update-available {version} —
    schema/installation-event.ts; publisher server/src/process.ts:115-117
    (updater callbacks).

## Phase 2 — publishers for the 14 types

- oc-core session/execution.rs: `session.status` {sessionID,status:{type:busy|idle}}
  published after session.execution.started / after each terminal execution
  event; `session.idle` {sessionID} alongside the idle status (deprecated
  frame, event-manifest.ts:74-77). Best-effort ephemeral.
- oc-core provider_catalog/refresh.rs: CatalogService::with_bus publishes
  `models-dev.refreshed` {} (global) after RefreshOutcome::Updated
  (models-dev.ts:416-422); SkippedDigest stays silent.
- oc-server handlers/credential.rs: credential.updated/switched on
  create/update/activate/remove with v2's exact pick ordering
  (desc(active),desc(time_created),desc(id)); replacement pick
  desc(time_created),desc(id); global routing.
- oc-server handlers/project.rs: `worktree.updated` {projectID} on
  row-owning create + successful remove (worktree.ts:131,228,270), routed
  to the project's location.
- oc-server announce.rs: location HEAD watcher (port of
  core/filesystem/location-watcher.ts) on the existing 250ms poll —
  publishes `filesystem.changed` {file,event:"change"} on HEAD change and
  `vcs.branch.updated` {branch} when the branch moved (vcs.ts:118-152).
- installation.*: oc-server announce::publish_installation_event (port of
  process.ts:115-117) + oc-cli autoupdate notice channel; serve drains it
  onto the in-process bus. serve.rs wiring, no-op elsewhere.

## Phase 3 — items 2-6

- item 2 (fork): handlers/session.rs fork rewritten — boundary located
  per ref session.ts:319-355 (before → that message, 404 when missing;
  else newest, 400 empty_session when none), instruction state + entry
  snapshot inherited, ONE durable session.forked event with the
  {type,messageID} boundary object (session-fork.ts:6-10); the
  pre-create + fake synthetic-item copies are GONE so project_fork
  (projector.rs:571) builds the row, copies settled history, fork-styles
  the title. Response = the projected row.
- item 3 (shell): handlers/session.rs shell rewritten per ref
  session/session.ts:179-222 + session/shell.ts — executes through the
  location Shell service (cwd=session dir, timeout 0, background
  metadata), publishes session.shell.started (event id = msg_→evt_) /
  session.shell.ended (1 MiB output preview), admits the
  ShellResult.userNotification synthetic with resume:false. The command
  text never reaches the model.
- item 5 (config.update): handlers/config.rs update wired to
  oc_core::config::update_shell (the jsonc_edit port; comment
  preservation), 204 on success — replaces the hardcoded 500.
- item 6 (info): /api/info body now carries
  capabilities.persistentPty (cfg!(not(windows)), ref
  binary.node.ts:2) — matches tools/parity/goldens/reference_api_info.json
  which already pins the field.
- item 4 (prompt/auto): oc-cli threads --prompt + effective auto into
  misc::root; forwarded via documented env contract
  OPENCODE_BOOT_PROMPT / OPENCODE_BOOT_AUTO (ruling: CLI side + env
  handoff, no oc-tui edits — BootArgs is TUI-lane owned).

